ants encoding several different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UNT1","text":"Small GTPase required for ciliation. Activated in a guanine nucleotide exchange factor (GEF)-independent manner via its intrinsic GDP for GTP nucleotide exchange ability (PubMed:28625565). Involved in ciliary assembly by binding the intraflagellar transport (IFT) complex B from the large pool pre-docked at the base of the cilium and thus triggers its entry into the cilia (PubMed:28428259, PubMed:28625565)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}